      "id": "adds-same-number",
      "objectiveId": "moe-math-g4-s1-p3-number-theory-and-fraction-obj5",
      "description": "Adds the same number to the top and bottom, thinking 1/2 = 2/3.",
      "response": "Fold or draw both fractions: 2/3 covers more of the strip than 1/2. Multiplying both parts keeps the amount the same; adding does not."
    },
    {
      "id": "bigger-numbers-bigger-fraction",
      "objectiveId": "moe-math-g4-s1-p3-number-theory-and-fraction-obj5",
      "description": "Thinks 4/8 is more than 1/2 because the numbers are bigger.",
      "response": "Line the strips up: 4/8 and 1/2 reach exactly the same point."
    }
  ],
